From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: C33 expectations

The per-target expectations upstream gives other ports:

- The PE core has no divide instructions; libgcc divides, and a zero
  divisor does not trap (20101011-1.c, as for csky and or1k).
- No MMU: a store through a null pointer does not fault, and mprotect
  cannot make a guard page.
- musl has no _FORTIFY_SOURCE functions, and its libm reports errors by
  exception only (math_errhandling 2).
- FDPIC code is always PIC, as ARM's, and -msep-data keeps the constant
  pool in .data.
- No conditional moves; the frame adds the 16-byte %r0-%r3 save block;
  the widening multiply is dumped as " w* "; a binary64 long double
  overflows at 1e4000L.
- Four and five megabytes in one piece, on the stack or in .bss, are more
  than a no-MMU process of 32 MB is given.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

